        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The summer is doing what summers do in Toronto - quieting the noise, but not the pressure. <strong>Andy O'Brien is in to run a rebuilt sport-performance department</strong>, a sharp organizational move that says the Leafs want sturdier legs, healthier bodies, and fewer excuses when camp opens. It fits a club that finished 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points and needs cleaner execution more than another round of excuses. Jack Roslovic sounds eager to rejoin Auston Matthews, and that matters; chemistry is cheaper than panic in August. Semyon Der-Arguchintsev still wants back in, another reminder that roster spots will be fought over, not handed out. <strong>Watch the fitness overhaul and the forward depth battle when camp arrives - those are the next real tests</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated August 4, 2026"
