      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Momentum is a fragile thing in August, but Toronto at least grabbed some of it back with <strong>Sunday's 3-1 win over the Astros</strong> - a tidy answer after Saturday's 5-1 loss to the Cardinals and a reminder that this club can still pitch and scratch enough offense to win a tight one. At 53-60, fifth in the AL East and 13.5 games back, the Blue Jays are no longer chasing the division so much as chasing respectability, but the recent 2-1 run against St. Louis and Houston has stopped the bleeding. The trade-deadline noise matters here too, because the front office has already made this a different roster. <strong>Tonight's rematch in Houston will show whether that hard-earned win was a spark or just a flicker.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated August 4, 2026"
      },
