      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The silence is the story now - and that's not a bad thing for a team trying to sort its spine. <strong>The Raptors' Kawhi Leonard trade is still on hold pending the NBA's investigation</strong>, the kind of front-office knot that keeps a summer conversation alive while the basketball calendar naps. Toronto sits 3rd in the Atlantic Division in the final ledger, but that number belongs to yesterday; the real issue is fit, not finish. The headline question is the same one that matters most in camp: can this roster find a floor-spacing center to open lanes for Scottie Barnes, whose open-trip accuracy will shape everything else? <strong>That answer - and whether Leonard ever officially lands in Toronto - is what will define the next turn of this offseason</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated August 4, 2026"
      },
